        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #31519.\">Fix</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2067036433\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/31519\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/31519/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/31519\">#31519</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I don't know C#; I don't know a lot of WebSocket. I think I'm on par in terms of knowledge with most of the maintainers here. This change was vibe-coded by Codex and I vibe-reviewed it and it looks correct enough and Claude agrees.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45472",
            "title": "Add method for sending messages to client in C# WS server",
