            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191840740?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds an explanation in the <code class=\"notranslate\">CustomElementRegistry.define()</code> documentation stating that existing elements in the document are automatically upgraded upon definition. It also adds a cross-reference link to <code class=\"notranslate\">CustomElementRegistry.upgrade()</code> under the \"See also\" section.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">When <code class=\"notranslate\">customElements.define()</code> is invoked, any matching elements that were previously parsed or inserted into the DOM are automatically upgraded by the browser (running their constructor and applicable lifecycle callbacks like <code class=\"notranslate\">connectedCallback()</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">attributeChangedCallback()</code>). Documenting this clarifies the lifecycle behavior for readers.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>WHATWG HTML Standard step for <code class=\"notranslate\">define()</code>: <a href=\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/custom-elements.html#dom-customelementregistry-define\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/custom-elements.html#dom-customelementregistry-define</a> (step 18)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #45241.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5192961243\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45241\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45241/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45241\">#45241</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45417",
            "title": "docs: note element upgrade step in CustomElementRegistry.define()",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-02T07:03:35.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-31T19:18:01.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "r4-rahul123",
                "url": "https://github.com/r4-rahul123"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">From Chrome 150 onwards, the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/zoom\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">zoom</code></a> CSS property is animatable; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5183671737909248\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5183671737909248</a>. It was always animatable in Firefox.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <a href=\"https://drafts.csswg.org/css-viewport/#zoom-property\" rel=\"nofollow\">spec</a> has been updated so that <code class=\"notranslate\">zoom</code> is now marked as animated by computed value type.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds animation details to the <code class=\"notranslate\">zoom</code> property page; I also took this opportunity to generally improve the page and make it follow the template.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
